{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6icvZ2dgFGpc6jgixL5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt` (lines 11-16): Order entity lacks status field\n- `OrderRepository.kt`: In-memory store with save/findById/findAll\n- `OrderController.kt`: POST create, GET by id, GET list endpoints\n- `Shipment.kt` (lines 9-27): Already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt`: In-memory store like OrderRepository\n- `ShipmentController.kt`: POST create, GET by id, GET list\n- `ApiExceptions.kt`: ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt` (line 31-37): ErrorCode enum with ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt`: Converts ApiException to ApiError response\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Spring Boot REST with MockMvc tests\n2. In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap\n3. Exception-based error handling (throw, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler)\n4. ResponseEntity controls HTTP status\n5. Tests assert status code, error code, and message\n6. Dependency injection of repositories into controllers\n\n**Affected files** (cannot be avoided):\n1. `Order.kt` — add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — implement POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel with business logic\n3. `ApiError.kt` — add error codes for order cancellation scenarios\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add method to find shipments by orderId\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — check order status when creating shipment\n6. Tests — verify cancel behavior across all cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Existing tests expect Order without status; adding it could break serialization or assertions\n- All-or-nothing semantics: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, cancel must fail and change nothing\n- Must find all shipments of an order to check their status before canceling\n- Retry safety: canceling already-CANCELLED order must succeed without changes\n\n**Open questions:** None. Ticket is clear on all behaviors.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED; add `status` field to Order data class, defaulting to ACTIVE\n   \n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise: sets order status to CANCELLED, saves it, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns order\n\n3. **ApiError.kt**: Add error codes for new failure cases:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` for 409 conflict when shipment is CONFIRMED\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to find all shipments for an order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In POST create, check if order exists and is CANCELLED; if CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with status 409\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling ACTIVE order returns 200 and CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling already-CANCELLED order returns 200 (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n   - Cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n   - Cancelling cancels CREATED shipments in the order\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for creating shipment on CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Having a service layer separate from controller: This would add complexity without solving the problem. The controllers are already thin and the business logic (checking shipments, updating multiple entities) is simple enough to keep in the controller while following existing patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with no shipments\n- Read order (exists, ACTIVE)\n- Find shipments for order (none)\n- Update order to CANCELLED\n- Return order with CANCELLED status\n- Status: 200 OK\n\nCase 2: Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments\n- Read order (exists, ACTIVE)\n- Find shipments for order\n- Check all shipments (none are CONFIRMED)\n- Update order to CANCELLED, update all shipments to CANCELLED\n- Return order with CANCELLED status\n- Status: 200 OK\n\nCase 3: Cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment\n- Read order (exists, ACTIVE)\n- Find shipments for order\n- Check shipment status (CONFIRMED found)\n- Throw ConflictException, no changes made\n- Response: {\"error\": {\"code\": \"ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\", \"message\": \"...\"}}\n- Status: 409 Conflict\n\nCase 4: Cancel CANCELLED order\n- Read order (exists, CANCELLED)\n- No changes needed\n- Return order (already CANCELLED)\n- Status: 200 OK\n\nCase 5: Cancel non-existent order\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException\n- Response: {\"error\": {\"code\": \"ORDER_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\"}}\n- Status: 404 Not Found\n\nCase 6: Create shipment for CANCELLED order\n- Read order (exists, CANCELLED)\n- Throw ConflictException (order is not ACTIVE)\n- Response: {\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_ORDER_CANCELLED\", \"message\": \"...\"}}\n- Status: 409 Conflict\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Cancel ACTIVE order successfully returns 200 and order is CANCELLED\n- Test 2: Cancelling already-CANCELLED order returns 200 (idempotent)\n- Test 3: Cancelling non-existent order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- Test 4: Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with appropriate code and order stays ACTIVE\n- Test 5: Cancelling ACTIVE order also cancels its CREATED shipments\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- Test 1: Creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":22108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1507},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a088650-0b06-4018-b749-9a724bc3e0a0","uuid":"4a6debda-21a8-4467-97df-9734ab1333da","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:24:32.369Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6icv5VyCKEqzGWnwp4T"}
