{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6imynVgrD7GKpCQAJSv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests passed: 19 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` passed with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 19 tests pass, including the original 12 baseline tests\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.cancel() and tested in `cancelling order also cancels its created shipments`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses ApiException hierarchy (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) handled by GlobalExceptionHandler, consistent with existing error patterns\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — All four cases tested:\n   - `cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent` — succeeds on retry\n   - `returns 409 when cancelling order with confirmed shipment` — changes nothing, order stays ACTIVE\n   - `returns 404 when cancelling a non-existent order` — refuses with 404\n   - `returns 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order` — refuses with 409\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified Kotlin source files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified order and shipment features and api package\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- `Order.kt` — Added OrderStatus enum and status field with default ACTIVE. This required change for the feature.\n- `OrderController.kt` — Added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository. Required to implement cancellation logic.\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Added findByOrderId() method to find shipme